.TH BOSWAS-SHELL 1 "November 2026" "Boswas OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
boswas-shell \- the Boswas OS desktop shell, lock screen and login screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/libexec/boswas/boswas-shell
[\fB\-\-lock\fR | \fB\-\-greeter\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-shell
draws the parts of the desktop that are not application windows. It is
started by
.BR boswas-compositor (1),
which gives it a trusted Wayland connection; it is not meant to be started
by hand. It is an ordinary, unprivileged process: if it exits, the
compositor starts it again and open windows are not affected.
.TP
(no option)
The desktop: the background, the panel along the bottom edge (launcher
button, pinned and running applications, network and battery status, clock)
and the launcher (search, all applications, lock, log out, restart, shut
down). Search is local: it matches installed applications and ranks them by
how often they were started. Restart, shut down and log out ask for a
second click.
.TP
.B \-\-lock
The lock screen. It shows the clock and asks for the password of the user
who owns the session, checked through PAM (service \fBboswas\-lock\fR). The
session is unlocked only after PAM accepts the password.
.TP
.B \-\-greeter
The login screen, run by
.BR greetd (1).
After a successful login greetd starts
.BR boswas-session (1)
for the user.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/boswas/launcher\-usage.json
How often each application was started from the launcher; used to rank
search results. It never leaves the device.
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/boswas\-lock
PAM service of the lock screen.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BOSWAS_LOG
Log filter (for example \fBdebug\fR). Messages go to standard error.
.TP
.B GREETD_SOCK
Set by greetd for the login screen.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas-compositor (1),
.BR boswas-session (1)
